? What is the central purpose of video editing?
+ Communicate the intended story
- Apply every available effect
- Remove every quiet moment
= Selection, order, pace and sound shape the message.

? What enables non-linear access to digital footage?
+ Random access storage
- Sequential tape copying
- Fixed broadcast order
= The editor can visit and rearrange clips without replaying all earlier material.

? What does a non-destructive editing project normally store?
+ Source references and edit decisions
- Only a finished flattened movie
- Only overwritten source frames
= The project records instructions while retaining source media.

? What is B-Roll in an interview-led video?
+ Relevant supporting footage
- The main spoken interview only
- An unrelated decorative title
= B-Roll shows relevant details while the main narrative can continue.

? Which cut starts the next sound before its picture?
+ J cut
- L cut
- Hard cut
= A J cut leads the next picture with its audio.

? Which cut continues earlier sound over the next picture?
+ L cut
- J cut
- Silent cut
= An L cut lets earlier audio continue beyond the picture boundary.

? What does a ripple edit commonly do to later material?
+ Shifts it with the duration change
- Overwrites all later source frames
- Keeps every later frame position
= A ripple change affects the downstream timeline position.

? Which shot best establishes the overall location?
+ Wide shot
- Extreme detail
- Tight insert
= A wide view provides spatial context.

? What is a dissolve transition?
+ A brief blend between pictures
- An immediate hard replacement
- A permanently frozen picture
= A dissolve overlaps the visible images for a period.

? Why check titles on a phone?
+ To verify small-screen readability
- To guarantee higher bit depth
- To remove the need for captions
= Text that looks readable on a large monitor may be too small on a phone.

? What is created by exporting the finished edit?
+ A playable delivery file
- Only the editable decision list
- A replacement camera recording
= Saving the project and exporting the movie serve different purposes.

? What should be checked after a compressed export?
+ The actual delivered picture and sound
- Only the editor preview thumbnail
- Only the project filename length
= The exported file can reveal errors not obvious in a preview.
